From: mini-router
Subject: spi: mt65xx: ignore an interrupt left pending by the previous kernel

A SPI-NAND operation still in flight when the running kernel kexecs into a new one completes after
the handover: its interrupt is pending when the new kernel requests the IRQ, the hard handler wakes
the thread (use_spimem is false before the first spi-mem op) and mtk_spi_interrupt_thread
dereferences cur_transfer, which is NULL:

  Unable to handle kernel read at virtual address 0000000000000010
  pc : mtk_spi_can_dma+0x0/0x30
  lr : mtk_spi_interrupt_thread+0x30/0x2ec

Clear the status while the clocks are on in probe, and treat an interrupt without a current transfer
as handled.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-mt65xx.c
@@ -885,6 +885,10 @@ static irqreturn_t mtk_spi_interrupt(int
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
+	/* no transfer in progress: stale, e.g. left over from before a kexec */
+	if (!mdata->cur_transfer)
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+
 	return IRQ_WAKE_THREAD;
 }
 
@@ -1304,6 +1308,9 @@ static int mtk_spi_probe(struct platform
 
 	mdata->spi_clk_hz = clk_get_rate(mdata->spi_clk);
 
+	/* reading the status clears an interrupt left pending by the previous (kexec) kernel */
+	readl(mdata->base + SPI_STATUS0_REG);
+
 	if (mdata->dev_comp->no_need_unprepare) {
 		clk_disable(mdata->spi_clk);
 		clk_disable(mdata->spi_hclk);
